course: dictionary
lesson: 5393
title: Meet the koala
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A koala is a grey, furry animal from Australia with big round ears and a black nose. It lives in eucalyptus trees and eats their leaves. «Koalas have fingerprints so like ours that they could confuse a detective.»
explain: Koalas are marsupials, like kangaroos. «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» The baby is called a joey, and it grows inside its mother's pouch.
explain: Many people call the koala a koala bear, but that is a wrong name. «The koala is no bear at all.» It is a marsupial, not a bear.
fact: A koala is a marsupial, so its baby grows in its mother's pouch.
fact: A baby koala is called a joey.
fact: Koalas eat eucalyptus leaves, and these leaves give them very little energy.
fact: Koalas sleep for many hours each day, often up to 20 hours.
fact: Koalas are threatened by bushfires and by the loss of trees.
exercise: «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» What is a marsupial? | An animal that lives only in the sea | A bear with a long tail | A tree that grows in Australia | *An animal whose babies grow in a pouch
exercise: What is a baby koala called? | A calf | A kitten | *A joey | A chick
exercise: What do koalas eat? | Bones and fur | Grass and seeds | Fish from the river | *Eucalyptus leaves
test: Which of these is a koala's home? | The bottom of the sea | *Eucalyptus trees in Australia | A dry lake bed in Africa | A cave in the desert
test: Why do koalas sleep so much? | They have to hunt at night | *Their leafy food gives them little energy | They are bored with their trees | They are sick
exam: Why is a koala not a bear, even though people call it a koala bear? | It has a long tail like a fox | It lives in the sea | It has no ears | *It is a marsupial, and its babies grow in a pouch
